<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hydra (island)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hydra is a Greek island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saronic-gulf">Saronic Gulf</a>, off the eastern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. In the 18th century its shipowners built a large merchant fleet, and during the Greek War of Independence from 1821 Hydriot ships formed the core of the Greek navy. Its car-free harbour town is now a well-known resort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hydra-greece.jpg" alt="Hydra (island)" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herbert Ortner, Vienna, Austria · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hydra_town_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
